[32m+[m[32m# Unimian identity decision[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mStatus: Accepted by the maintainer on 2026-09-29. Local preparation only.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Decision[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe product formerly named **Wise View** is rebranded as **Unimian**.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m| Surface | Current value | Unimian value |[m
[32m+[m[32m| --- | --- | --- |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Display name | `Wise View` | `Unimian` |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Obsidian plugin ID and install folder | `wise-view` | `unimian` |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Package name | `obsidian-wise-view` | `obsidian-unimian` |[m
[32m+[m[32m| GitHub repository target | `parkisutama/obsidian-wise-view` | `parkisutama/obsidian-unimian` |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Release archive | `wise-view.zip` | `unimian.zip` |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Bases view ID prefix | `wise-view-*` | `unimian-*` |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Plugin CSS class and variable prefix | `wise-view-*` | `unimian-*` |[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe plugin is being prepared locally. Do not rename the GitHub repository, push, publish a release, submit to the Obsidian Community Directory, or deploy to an operational vault as part of this decision.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Scope and invariants[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- Replace the active product name, repository references, package identity, install-folder guidance, and release archive name.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Keep the existing product positioning and feature set. The rebrand does not change view behavior, editor behavior, plugin settings schema, or note/frontmatter data.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Rename registered Bases view IDs and CSS hooks to the `unimian-*` prefix. No vault `.base` files are changed as part of local preparation; any existing view type references need manual updating if they are used.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Keep stored view option keys unchanged so existing view settings retain their shape when a `.base` file uses a renamed view type.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Keep third-party license terms, copyright notices, and source attribution intact; update only references to the current product identity.[m
[32m+[m[32m- No note/frontmatter data or settings-schema migration is required. If an existing `.base` file[m
[32m+[m[32m  stores an old view type, change that type to its `unimian-*` ID manually; the plugin does not[m
[32m+[m[32m  register aliases for the old IDs. The maintainer is the only current user.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Preserve the current version metadata during local preparation. Choose a release version when a release is authorized; its tag must match `manifest.json`.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Obsidian directory constraints for a future submission[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- The plugin ID must be unique, use lowercase letters and hyphens, and must not contain `obsidian`. The install folder must match the ID.[m
[32m+[m[32m- The display name must be unique and must not contain `Obsidian` or `Plugin`.[m
[32m+[m[32m- The manifest description must be no longer than 250 characters and end with a period.[m
[32m+[m[32m- A directory submission requires the final manifest on the default branch and a GitHub release with a matching version tag and the required plugin assets.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Submit through the Obsidian Community Directory flow when publication is later authorized.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Historical identifiers[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe old `wise-view-*` identifiers are retained only in historical notes and in the old-to-new mapping above. They are no longer registered by Unimian.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mHistorical task reports and the license-compliance plan retain the Wise View name where it records the identity used at the time. Update active product documentation and runtime copy; do not rewrite historical acceptance evidence.[m
